Keep a failed decoder setup failed.

Our own patch (AvP). This bug is in libvorbis 1.3.7. Upstream's main no longer has it:
its codebook rewrite (ec9ca811) frees the decode books on failure, and that rewrite
cannot be taken on its own. When building the decode books failed, the half-built
list stayed in place, so the next ov_read reported success and decoded with books of
dimension 0. A crafted file gets there with no shortage of memory: an impossible
Huffman tree in book 0 is enough. It then crashed on a division by zero in res0.c, or
hung in floor 0.

--- a/lib/block.c
+++ b/lib/block.c
@@ -284,6 +284,14 @@ static int _vds_shared_init(vorbis_dsp_state *v,vorbis_info *vi,int encp){
 
   return 0;
  abort_books:
+  /* A setup that fails must stay failed, because the caller can simply try
+     again: ov_read does, every time it is called. So nothing half built may
+     be left behind. The static books and the half built decode books all go,
+     and the next try comes straight back here, because it finds no static book
+     to build from. (Before, the next try found fullbooks already there, took
+     that to mean the books were ready and reported success. The failed book and
+     those after it were all zeros, so decoding audio divided by a dim of 0 in
+     res0.c, or hung in floor 0.) */
   for(i=0;i<ci->books;i++){
     if(ci->book_param[i]!=NULL){
       vorbis_staticbook_destroy(ci->book_param[i]);
@@ -291,6 +299,12 @@ static int _vds_shared_init(vorbis_dsp_state *v,vorbis_info *vi,int encp){
     }
   }
   vorbis_dsp_clear(v);
+  if(ci->fullbooks!=NULL){
+    for(i=0;i<ci->books;i++)
+      vorbis_book_clear(ci->fullbooks+i);
+    _ogg_free(ci->fullbooks);
+    ci->fullbooks=NULL;
+  }
   return -1;
 }
 
